<rdf:label>AtomicOperationalMktPlan An AtomicOperationalMktPlan corresponds to a campaign plan which is the smallest level of the OperationalMarketingPlan hierarchy.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeOperationalMktPlan -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeOperationalMktPlan">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>CompositeOperationalMktPlan A Composite OperationalMktPlan corresponds to several OperationalMktPlan items that are associated together within in the same OperationalMktPlan.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketStrategy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketStrategy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>MarketStrategy A carefully devised plan of action on how to address the market with appropriate ProductOfferings and SalesChannesl.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#OperationalMarketingPlan -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#OperationalMarketingPlan">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>OperationalMarketingPlan An OperationalMarketingPlan defines the long-term or middle-term Marketing strategy for product placement.

The OperationalMarketingPlan is an abstract class that defines the hierarchical view of a package of OperationalMarketingPlan item.

It may be: A Composite OperationalMktPlan corresponding to several OperationalMktPlan items that are associated together within in the same marketing program. An Atomic OperationalMktPlan corresponding to a campaign plan which is the smallest level of the OperationalMarketingPlan hierarchy.

Marketing Plan is a Composite OperationalMktPlan composed of Marketing Programs

Marketing Program is a Composite OperationalMktPlan composed of Campaign Plans

A Marketing Campaign is associated to a Campaign Plan that is an AtomicOperationalMktPlan.

An OperationalMarketingPlan specifies the Budget allocated, forcasted and achieved,

         the targeted Parties (PartyProfile and PartyProfileType),

         the SaleChannel to be used,

         the ProductSpecification, ProductSpecificationType, CommercialClassification and ProductOffering it gives away or aims to place,

         the MarketingCampaignRoles involved,

         and the MarketingObjectives that must be achieved including the indicators used to evaluate the achievement (MktIndicatorSpec)</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Market and Sales Domain.Marketing Campaign ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Market and Sales Domain.Marketing Campaign ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicMarketingCampaignCharacteristic"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeMarketingCampaignCharacteristic"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingCampaign"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingCampaignCharacteristic"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingCampaignCharacteristicValue"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MktCampaignRule"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MktCampaignWave"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WaveList"/>
<rdf:label>Market and Sales Domain.Marketing Campaign ABE The Marketing Campaign ABE represents the strategy, or approach, for marketing new or existing ProductOfferings to identified target markets. The campaign could be for one of the following:

         The launch of a pre-paid ProductOffering with multiple promotions across SalesChannels, MarketSegments, and so forth

         A new campaign for an existing ProductOffering; the ProductOffering is not new, but the relationships, collateral, and so forth could be new

         A re-launch of a campaign for an existing ProductOffering</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicMarketingCampaignCharacteristic -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicMarketingCampaignCharacteristic">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#derivationFormula"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#extensible"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#maxCardinality"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#minCardinality"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unique"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#valueType"/>
<rdf:label>AtomicMarketingCampaignCharacteristic A type of MarketingCampaignCharacteristic that does not have any subordinate MarketingCampaignCharacteristics, that is, an AtomicMarketingCampaignCharacteristic is a leaf-level MarketingCampaignCharacteristic.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeMarketingCampaignCharacteristic -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeMarketingCampaignCharacteristic">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#derivationFormula"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#extensible"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#maxCardinality"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#minCardinality"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unique"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#valueType"/>
<rdf:label>CompositeMarketingCampaignCharacteristic A type of MarketingCampaignCharacteristic that is formed by aggregating other MarketingCampaignCharacteristic, which may be Composite or Atomic MarketingCampaignCharacteristic.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingCampaign -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingCampaign">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#excutionPeriod"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#mcType"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>MarketingCampaign MarketingCampaigns promote a product through different media, including television, radio, print and online platforms. Campaigns dont have to rely solely on advertising and can also include demonstrations, word of mouth and other interactive techniques. Businesses operating in highly competitive markets may initiate frequent marketing campaigns and devote significant resources to generating brand awareness and sales.

Marketing campaigns can be designed with different goals in mind, including building a brand image, introducing a new product, increasing sales of a product already on the market, or even reducing the impact of negative news. Defining a campaigns goal usually dictates how much marketing is needed and what media are most effective.

A MarketingCampaign specifies

         the Budget allocated, forcasted and achieved,

         the targeted Parties (PartyProfile),

         the SaleChannel and the CommunicationMode or Media to be used,

         the ProductSpecification and ProductOffering it gives away or aims to place,

         the creative used during the campaign (Document and DocumentSpecification),

         and the MktCampaignRules such as rules that will be evaluated for triggering an event-based Marketing Campaign.

A MarketingCampaign is managed by a MktCampaigneManager and designed by a MktCampaignOperator.

A MarketingCampaign is split into waves (MktCampaignWave).

A Marketing Campaign is described in a marketing campaign brief (Document) which describes all the information required to prepare the campaign.

The brief puts the campaign into context and sets campaign objectives. It brings together the information necessary to create a campaign:

         Campaign objectives which are the smallest level of the hierarchy of marketing objectives. They deal with the selected actions to attempt to reach the marketing objectives defined at the Marketing plan level (e.g. action such as sale of an option, stimulate usage, retain with promotions, sale of a mobile or accessories, optimize ARPU, );

         Metrics and KPIs to measure the performance of a campaign based on MktIndicatorSpec referring to quantitative data such as proposition take rate or click-through objectives for example (achieve a click-through rate of 4% or higher, achieve a proposition take rate of 1.5% or higher, .);

         a target market which is composed by party segments;

         a message based on a general idea or sentence that summarises what you want to say to the customers;

         a budget which is the smallest part of a marketing plan budget allocated at a campaign;

         propositions based on offer specification or/and product specification.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingCampaignCharacteristic -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingCampaignCharacteristic">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#derivationFormula"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#extensible"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#maxCardinality"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#minCardinality"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unique"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#valueType"/>
<rdf:label>MarketingCampaignCharacteristic A characteristic quality or distinctive feature of a MarketingCampaign. The characteristic can be take on a discrete value, such as number of press releases, can take on a range of values, (for example, number of prospects reached 50,000 - 100,000), or can be derived from a formula (for example, number of brokerage house pickups = sum of all brokerage house instance characteristics).</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingCampaignCharacteristicValue -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingCampaignCharacteristicValue">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#fromValue"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isDefault"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#rangeInterval"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#toValue"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unitOfMeasure"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#value"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#valueType"/>
<rdf:label>MarketingCampaignCharacteristicValue A number or text that can be assigned to a MarketingCampaignCharacteristic.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MktCampaignRule -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MktCampaignRule">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasSubRules"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isCNF"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isMandatoryEvaluation"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#usage"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#keywords"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#policyName"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>MktCampaignRule </rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MktCampaignWave -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MktCampaignWave">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>MktCampaignWave In a multichannel campaign management system, marketing campaign management requires to subdivide a campaign in several marketing campaign wave. A marketing campaign wave should use one communication mode and one target. It could be outbound or inbound.

The MktCampaignWave is the smallest operational subdivision of a campaign, with a unique target (set of segmentation criteria to define which persons or legal entities to reach), unique interaction channel (1014, 3000, external call-center), media (ads in a newspaper, ads in the subway), a duration. It may be inbound (people try to reach the CSP) or outbound (te CSP tries to reach them).</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WaveList -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WaveList">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#dateCreated"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#respectsThreshold"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>WaveList A WaveList corresponds to the split of a MarketingCampaigns target in waves. The reason of the split might be:

         temporal splitting: wave recurrence, (ex: a non-recurrent Wave has only one Waves Recurrence);

         technical splitting (ex: limited volume in email sending, SMS sending).</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Market and Sales Domain.Marketing Performance ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Market and Sales Domain.Marketing Performance ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingIndicator"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingIndicatorDefinition"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingObjectiveDefinition"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingObjectiveMeasure"/>
<rdf:label>Market and Sales Domain.Marketing Performance ABE Marketing Performance ABE contains all information used to define Marketing and Sales performance objectives and Marketing indicators measured.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingIndicator -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingIndicator">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#value"/>
<rdf:label>MarketingIndicator A MarketingIndicator is a type of MetricMeasure described by MarketingIndicatorDefinition that contains the result of MarketingIndicatorDefinitions evaluation for an instance of Entity for a specific period.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingIndicatorDefinition -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingIndicatorDefinition">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#accuracy"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#captureFrequency"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#captureMethod"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#capturePeriod"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unitOfMeasure"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#valueType"/>
<rdf:label>MarketingIndicatorDefinition A MarketingIndicatorDefinition specifies a metric measure. It specifies measure (how to calculate it) with targeted values and associated actions when the thresholds arent achieved. 

The MarketingIndicatorDefinitions are used to define objectives of OperationalMarketingPlans and MarketingCampaigns such as performance or budget objectives.

MarketingIndicatorDefinition is a type of MetricDefMeasure.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingObjectiveDefinition -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingObjectiveDefinition">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#collectionType"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#entryDate"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#lastUsed"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#metricLevel"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#perspective"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>MarketingObjectiveDefinition MarketingObjectiveDefinition is a set of actions in charge of to specify, CSP communications and presence according to strategic axes, to support product introductions and specific promotions to sell products, retain customers, and bring in new customers.

Example:

         drive profitable sales with marketing objectives such as sell on value, promote strategic products, improve sales cycle

         grow customer profitability with marketing objectives such as retain and grow strategic accounts, customer PandL sales focus

MarketingObjectiveDefinition is defined by metrics to evaluate with threshold that must be achieved and possibly actions that must be applied when the thresholds are not achieved. These metrics and thresholds are specified with MktIndicatorDefinition.

MarketingObjectiveDefinition is a type of MetricDefinition.

Each MarketingObjectiveDefinition might take part in one or many MarketingObjectiveDefinitions.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingObjectiveMeasure -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketingObjectiveMeasure">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#observationPeriod"/>
<rdf:label>MarketingObjectiveMeasure </rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Market and Sales Domain.Sales Commission ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Market and Sales Domain.Sales Commission ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommission"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommissionRule"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommissionSpecification"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommissionSpecificationType"/>
<rdf:label>Market and Sales Domain.Sales Commission ABE The Sales Commission ABE contains all Business Entities used to specify commissions for Sales Agent, Employees... including commission rules and commissions applied.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommission -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommission">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#value"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>SalesCommission SalesCommission represents a form of remuneration (fixed value, percentage or formula) for services rendered or products sold by a sales agent.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommissionRule -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommissionRule">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasSubRules"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isCNF"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isMandatoryEvaluation"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#usage"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#keywords"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#policyName"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>SalesCommissionRule A SalesCommissionRule is a type of PolicyRule. The SalesCommissionRule is used to add complex rule, as the formula supplied as part of the SalesCommissionSpecification is simple in nature. The SalesCommissionRule specifies:

              Events triggering the evaluation of the rule (Sales Events)

                  Ex: Every first of a month, on reaching a predefined amount of sale or on the request of an employee/agent

              Conditions that need to be checked

                  Ex: If the invoice amount is above 100 $, If more than 2 hours of international call etc.,

              Actions that should be performed if the condition clause is evaluated to TRUE 

                  Ex: Calculate the Sales Commission based upon percentage of the Sales Value.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommissionSpecification -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommissionSpecification">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#formula"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#value"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>SalesCommissionSpecification The SalesCommissionSpecification represents a sales commission specification as perceived by the business user and specifies how the commission is calculated at a functional level (i.e. what are the rules, which conditions are applicable).

The commission might be a fixed value, a percentage or even a more complex formula.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommissionSpecificationType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesCommissionSpecificationType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>SalesCommissionSpecificationType A SalesCommissionSpecificationType is a type of EntitySpecificationType and represents a classification that groups SalesCommissionSpecification that share common characteristics. For e.g. SalesCommissionSpefication Sales is composed of different Sales Categories Handset, Accessories etc.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Sales Lead and Opportunity ABE.Sales Opportunity ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Sales Lead and Opportunity ABE.Sales Opportunity ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesOpportunity"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesOpportunityItem"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesProject"/>
<rdf:label>Sales Lead and Opportunity ABE.Sales Opportunity ABE Sales Opportunity ABE provides the ability to track pending deals and the amount of potential revenue the leads represent in the form of a sales pipeline including proposals made to potential customers.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesOpportunity -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesOpportunity">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#frequency"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#value"/>
<rdf:label>SalesOpportunity A SalesOpportunity is an opportunity to generate revenue from a SalesLead that can already be an existing Customer. Opportunities are the pending deals that need to be tracked. Opportunities build the pipeline, which will contribute to the forecast. A SalesOpportunity represents an interest expressed by a Party known as a SalesLead to at least one ProductOffering/ProductSpecification proposed by the CSP.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesOpportunityItem -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesOpportunityItem">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#value"/>
<rdf:label>SalesOpportunityItem A SalesOpportunityItem is the smallest entity in a SalesOpportunity. Each SalesOpportunityItem details a wished ProductOffering of the Prospect.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesProject -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesProject">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#assumptions"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#constraints"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#exclusions"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#inclusions"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#projectNr"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#title"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#versionNr"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#actualDuration"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ACWP"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BCWP"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BCWS"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#currentDuration"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#plannedDuration"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#priority"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#scheduledDuration"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#timingConstraint"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#timingConstraintDate"/>
<rdf:label>SalesProject A SalesProject is a type of Project which achieves a business goal in the context of a sale and concerns a SalesOpportunity. The aims of a SalesProject is to detail the need of the Prospect up to lead to Agreement(s) and / or CustomerProductOrders.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Sales Lead and Opportunity ABE.Sales Lead ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Sales Lead and Opportunity ABE.Sales Lead ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesLead"/>
<rdf:label>Sales Lead and Opportunity ABE.Sales Lead ABE Sales Lead ABE provides the ability to track sales leads through their lifecycle up until the time the prospect becomes a customer.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesLead -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SalesLead">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>SalesLead The SalesLead corresponds to the nominal result of an interaction involving a Prospect towards one of our offers (the first stage (S) of the SPANCO process).

In a nominal way, once the interest towards ours offers is confirmed and the Prospect is clearly identified, then an Opportunity might be created.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Market and Sales Domain.Market Sales Statistics ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Market and Sales Domain.Market Sales Statistics ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicMarketStatistic"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeMarketStatistic"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketStatistic"/>
<rdf:label>Market and Sales Domain.Market Sales Statistics ABE The Market Sales Statistics maintains market and sales key performance indicators about Sales and Marketing revenue and sales channel performance.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicMarketStatistic -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicMarketStatistic">
