</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServiceDefinition -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServiceDefinition">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#activationMode"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#sdStatus"/>
<rdf:label>ServiceDefinition Represents a type of Service Specification introduced for the purposes of Service Fulfillment. It defines ALL the ServiceSpecCharacteristics (SSCs) that must be used to create corresponding Service instances. This includes the SSCs which are: 
globally set (the corresponding values are defined only in ServiceTemplates and are sometimes designated as invariant) and 
set per instance (since the ServiceDefinition does not contain any value for such SSCs, the corresponding values can be defined only over the Activation Interface and are sometimes designated as variant)</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServiceTemplate -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServiceTemplate">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#serviceLocation"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#source"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#stStatus"/>
<rdf:label>ServiceTemplate Represents a type of Service Specification introduced for the purposes of Service Fulfillment. It defines specific ServiceSpecCharacteristicsValues for the globally set ServiceSpecCharacteristics that can be dynamically referenced by multiple Service instances during their lifecycle span. A ServiceTemplate is checked against its associated ServiceDefinition by verifying the presence of the ServiceSpecCharacteristics and the validity of the corresponding assigned ServiceSpecCharacteristicsValues.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Resource Domain -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Resource Domain">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdf:label>Business Entity.Resource Domain Resource Domain Executive Summary
Part of this document describes Computing and Software Resources within the Resource domain of the Information Framework (SID).  Included is support for digital services, such as Workplace as a Service (WpaaS), multi-tenancy offerings, support for virtualization and network resource abstraction by the introduction of the Resource Function concept.
The move to virtualization, hybrid networks using both traditional Network Appliances and Network Applications software running on virtual machines or container technologies introduces a much more dynamic relationship between the network capabilities and how they are realized at any instance in time by resources.
The introduction of the Concept of Network as a Service promoted in TMF909 NaaS API Component Suite [1] and Open Digital Architecture (ODA) GB999 ODA Production Implementation Guidelines [2] - introduces the notion of abstracting network capabilities by separating the What is provided, from How it is provided. This allows uniform network services to be defined independent of specific technologies and their realization which may not be known at design time. Example of where this is useful for 5G/4G based services where the switch from 4G to 5G access needs to be transparent to the consumer of the Network Service. 
Evolution of Network implementations from network appliances to network applications as software running on compute infrastructure requires adjustment to the traditional resource management models which reflect static assets that take time to deploy and configure, and which change infrequently to a model that can handle dynamic run time change in these relationships such as encountered with Network Function Virtualization (NFV).
Computing Resources, while not explicitly modelled, are supported by a number of SID Aggregate Business Entities (ABEs) including Physical Resource Specification, Logical Resource Specification, Compound Resource Specification, and their related entity ABEs, such as Physical Resource.
Software Resources are explicitly modelled within the SID and supported by a number of current ABEs, including Logical Resource Specification, Software, and Operating System.
The Compound Resource Specification, Compound Resource, Software ABEs have been enhanced.  The Operating System ABE is now supported by the Software Specification and Software ABEs and has therefore been removed.
Support for a number of scenarios, which includes, but is not limited to, Software compatibility and WpaaS, and vCPE are also contained within this document.
Resource Domain Overviews
The Resource domain represents roles, information and activities carried out by parties (e.g. individuals / organizations) playing roles that are involved in the strategic planning, definition, development and operational aspects of Resources (e.g. functions, applications, computing, networking and storage) that represent the infrastructure of an enterprise that are used to realize Services. Activities include management of: strategies, capabilities, lifecycles, catalogs, inventories, topologies, installations, activations, alarms, problems, performance, mediation, usage statistics and support of Resources that are managed by an enterprise.

The Resource Domain provides a view of the resource portion of the information model, which includes mined information from other information models. The SID draws from the work of ITU-T, IETF, ONF, MEF and DMTF. This model is built with the express purpose of serving as a foundation for other Resource (sub-) models to fit into.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Resource Domain.Resource Party Roles ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Resource Domain.Resource Party Roles ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceInstaller"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Technician"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TelecomTechnician"/>
<rdf:label>Resource Domain.Resource Party Roles ABE Resource Party Roles ABE contains all PartyRoles related to the Resource Domain such as Technician, ResourceManager. </rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceInstaller -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceInstaller">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceInstaller An individual who installs PhysicalResources. It specifically doesnt provide all of the capabilities of a Technician role, but also represents a less costly PartyRole. Specifically, a ResourceInstaller is limited to simple physical installation of Equipment. A ResourceInstaller does not configure Resources or Services. </rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Technician -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Technician">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>Technician An individual who possesses specific technical training and competence in a specific area, such as digital services.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TelecomTechnician -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TelecomTechnician">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>TelecomTechnician An individual who possesses specific technical training and competence in telecommunications.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Resource Domain.Resource Specification ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Resource Domain.Resource Specification ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceRoleSpecification"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharacteristic"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharacteristicValue"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharUse"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharValueUse"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecification"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecificationPerfRole"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecificationRelationship"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecificationType"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecVersion"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecVersionDetails"/>
<rdf:label>Resource Domain.Resource Specification ABE The Resource Specification ABE contains entities that define the shared characteristics and behavior of each of the four types of Resource entities. This enables multiple instances to be derived from a single specification entity. In this derivation, each instance will use the shared characteristics and behavior defined in its associated template.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceRoleSpecification -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceRoleSpecification">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceRoleSpecification This is the abstract base class for all ResourceRoleSpecification subclasses. It exists to enable relationships to be defined between it and other classes in the model. This helps prevent relationship explosion. It is used to define the invariant attributes, methods, relationships, and constraints of various types of roles associated with Resources (both physical and logical) in the model.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharacteristic -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharacteristic">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#derivationFormula"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#extensible"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#maxCardinality"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#minCardinality"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unique"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#valueType"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecCharacteristic A characteristic quality or distinctive feature of a ResourceSpecification. The characteristic can be take on a discrete value, such as color, can take on a range of values, (for example, sensitivity of 100-240 mV), or can be derived from a formula (for example, usage time (hrs) = 30 - talk time *3). Certain characteristics, such as color, may be configured during the ordering or some other process.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharacteristicValue -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharacteristicValue">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#attribute1"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isDefault"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#rangeInterval"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#rangeStep"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unitOfMeasure"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#value"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#valueFrom"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#valueTo"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#valueType"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecCharacteristicValue A number or text that can be assigned to a ResourceSpecCharacteristic.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharUse -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharUse">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#canBeOverridden"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#extensible"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isPackage"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#maxCardinality"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#minCardinality"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unique"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecCharUse A use of the ResourceSpecCharacteristic by an ServiceSpecification to which additional properties (attributes) apply or override the properties of similar properties contained in ResourceSpecCharacteristic.This aggregation defines the set of characteristics, or distinguishing features, of a particular ResourceSpecification.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharValueUse -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecCharValueUse">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isDefault"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecCharValueUse A use of theResourceSpecCharacteristicValue by an EntitySpecification to which additional properties (attributes) apply or override the properties of similar properties contained in ResourceSpecCharacteristicValue.This association defines the allowed set of values (represented as instances of the ResourceSpecCharacteristicValue object) that a specific ResourceSpecification can have when that ResourceSpecification object is instantiated.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecification -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecification">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecification ResourceSpecification is an abstract base class that is used to define the invariant characteristics and behavior (attributes, methods, constraints, and relationships) of a managed or unmanaged Resource.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecificationPerfRole -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecificationPerfRole">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#roleType"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecificationPerfRole A role that a ResourceSpecification plays in defining a PerformanceSpecification.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecificationRelationship -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecificationRelationship">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecificationRelationship A migration, substitution, dependency, or exclusivity relationship between/among ResourceSpecifications.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecificationType -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecificationType">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecificationType A ResourceSpecificationType entity is used to categorize sets of ResourceSpecifications.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecVersion -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecVersion">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#format"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#number"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#reason"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#semantics"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#timestamp"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecVersion This class represents the ability to distinguish between different instances of ResourceSpecifications. It represents a particular form or variety of a ResourceSpecification that is different from others or from the original. The form represents differences in attributes, methods, relationships, and/or constraints that characterize this particular ResourceSpecification, but which are not enough to warrant creating a new ResourceSpecification.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecVersionDetails -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceSpecVersionDetails">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#minVersionForUse"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#preferredVersionToUse"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceSpecVersionDetails This class defines the semantics of the modifiesResourceSpec aggregation. Specifically, it enables an application to define which set of versions of this ResourceSpecification are appropriate for a given task.This aggregation represents the set of versions of this ResourceSpecification. The semantics of this aggregation are implemented with the ResourceSpecVersionDetails class.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Resource Specification ABE.CompoundResource Specification ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Resource Specification ABE.CompoundResource Specification ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompoundResourceSpec"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SoftBlackBoxSpecification"/>
<rdf:label>Resource Specification ABE.CompoundResource Specification ABE The CompoundResource Specification ABE used to define the invariant characteristics and behavior (attributes, methods, constraints, and relationships) of a CompoundResource.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompoundResourceSpec -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompoundResourceSpec">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>CompoundResourceSpec The CompoundResourceSpec used to define the invariant characteristics and behavior (attributes, methods, constraints, and relationships) of a CompoundResource.

The key difference between a CompoundResourceSpec and either a PhysicalResourceSpec and a LogicalResourceSpec is that a PhysicalResourceSpec and LogicalResourceSpec define templates for specifying the invariant characteristics and behavior of PhysicalResources and LogicalResources, respectively. Optionally, one or more CompoundResourceSpecs may also be specified.

Thus, a CompoundResourceSpec is in effect a "shorthand notation" for specifying complementary PhysicalResourceSpecs and / or LogicalResourceSpecs.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

