<rdf:label>SNMPMethod This is an abstract base class for defining different types of SNMP methods to perform various FCAPS functions.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SupportedMgmtMethodDetail -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SupportedMgmtMethodDetail">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#preferredConfigMethod"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#preferredMonitorMethod"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#supportedMgmtMethods"/>
<rdf:label>SupportedMgmtMethodDetail This is an association class, and defines the semantics of the SupportedMgmtMethods aggregation. This enables different management methods (e.g., CLI vs. SNMP) to be used to perform configuration versus monitoring functions.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TL1Method -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TL1Method">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>TL1Method This is an abstract base class for defining different types of TL1 methods to perform various FCAPS functions.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Management Information ABE.Performance Info ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Management Information ABE.Performance Info ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PerformanceInfo"/>
<rdf:label>Management Information ABE.Performance Info ABE </rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PerformanceInfo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PerformanceInfo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#mgmtInfoValidFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#retrievalMethodCurrent"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#retrievalMethodsSupported"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>PerformanceInfo PerformanceInfo is the base class for all performance monitoring classes. Resource Performance is the act of collecting, correlating, consolidating, and validating various performance statistics and other operational characteristics of PhysicalResource, LogicalResource, CompoundResource, and Network entities. Service Performance is similar, except that it applies to CustomerFacingServices and ResourceFacingServices. Both of these entities also include specific subclasses for conducting network performance assessment against planned goals, performs various aspects of trend analysis, including error rate and cause analysis and Resource degradation.

Different types of performance indicators are associated with a particular Resource or Service using the DescribedByMgmtInfo aggregation. Performance information Subclasses of this class define the detailed characteristics and behavior of this class. Performance monitors are reported by associating the parent of this class, ManagementInfo, with the ManagementMethodEntity class through a combination of the DescribedByMgmtInfo and the MgmtInfoObtainedBy aggregation.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Management Information ABE.Resource State ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Management Information ABE.Resource State ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceStateInfo"/>
<rdf:label>Management Information ABE.Resource State ABE </rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceStateInfo -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceStateInfo">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#mgmtInfoValidFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#retrievalMethodCurrent"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#retrievalMethodsSupported"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceStateInfo ResourceStateInfo is an abstract base class for representing different types of management information that describes the state of a particular Resource.

Subclasses of this class include classes to represent Faults, Outages, Alarms, the usage of this Resource, and its current operational state.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Management Information ABE.Resource Statistical ABE -->

