<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>ASIC An ASIC is an Application Specific Integrated Circuit.

This class represents a special type of Chip that is used to upgrade the functionality of a networking device. Examples include upgrading the modem function of a device, increasing the processing capability of a Card or Device, and implementing some type of networking functionality, such as fast switching, directly in hardware (as opposed to emulating it in software).</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

