</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PortabilityRequestPolicyRule -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PortabilityRequestPolicyRule">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>PortabilityRequestPolicyRule PortabilityRequestPolicyRule is the associated Class for the relationship of many-to-many between NumberPortabilityRequest and NumberPortabilityPolicyRule. Through this class, the relation combined of the both of them is stored.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Resource Order ABE.Resource Number Portability Role ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Resource Order ABE.Resource Number Portability Role ABE">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#NumberPortabilityClearinghouse"/>
<TMF_v1:hasBE rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#NumberPortabilityRole"/>
<rdf:label>Resource Order ABE.Resource Number Portability Role ABE The Resource Number Portability Role ABE contains entities related to the roles taked for the portability.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#NumberPortabilityClearinghouse -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#NumberPortabilityClearinghouse">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>NumberPortabilityClearinghouse Sub-class of PartyRole. Its the administrator of all number portability and the main center point for all the messages sent.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#NumberPortabilityRole -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#NumberPortabilityRole">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#portabilityStatus"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#roleCombination"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#roleSelectionMethod"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>NumberPortabilityRole This class gives a specific behavior and responsibilities to the requests, depending of many factors and the source provided. It has a portabilityStatus as a specific attribute and a generalization to an existing entity called LogicalResourceRole. This entity helps with the management and tracking of the status for the portability requests, since it can be initiated, started, completed, among others. This track is made for the requests through the continuous communications with other sources, like the entities Number Portability Clearinghouse and External System as party roles. Therefore, NumberPortability, because of its complexity, its management of different states between its flow with other sources, works with a NumberPortabilityRole through an aggregation. All the number portability requests have a behavior with an affinity and dependency to the different parties created and added. (NP Clearinghouse, External System, Customer). This relation affects directly to the tracking for the portability through a status. For this weve created the specific attribute "portabilityStatus" for the entity "NumberPortabilityRole". Example:

PartyRole (
Customer:
NumberPortabilityRole (
portabilityStatus : created
)
NumberPortabilityClearinghouse:
NumberPortabilityRole (
portabilityStatus : accepted
)

)</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Resource Domain.Resource Usage ABE -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Resource Domain.Resource Usage ABE">
