<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProjectElementSpec -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProjectElementSpec">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#expectedDuration"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdf:label>ProjectElementSpec Specifies characteristics that apply to types of ProjectElements. This is an abstract entity used to hold the attributes and associations common to ProjectSpecification, WBS ElementSpecification and ActivitySpecification. These entities can be used to build standard project templates to aid in Project creation.</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProjectElementRelationship -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProjectElementRelationship">
<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#dependencyLag"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#dependencyLead"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#replacementDate"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#subType"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<TMF_v1:hasAttribute rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>ProjectElementRelationship ·         The ProjectElementRelationship allows relating ProjectElements. A ProjectElement might be linked to several ProjectElements.
Ex: a ProjectElement not being able to start until another ProjectElement has been completed.
The ProjectElements can be related by two types of relationships: Dependency or Replacement.
A Dependency is where the two Project Elements have some starting or finishing dependency. E.g. Activity 2 cannot start until Activity 1 is complete.
A Replacement is where one or more ProjectElements are replaced by one or more other ProjectElements.
Each type of relationship might be subdivided into several kinds: 
The subtypes of Dependency are:
before-start-delay: Activity2 starts at least lag timepoints after Activity1 starts
before-finish-delay: Activity2 starts at least lag timepoints after Activity1 finishes
after-start-delay: Activity2 finishes at least lag timepoints after Activity1 starts
after-finish-delay: Activity2 finishes at least lag timepoints after Activity1 finishes
start-equal-start: Activity2 starts exactly lag timepoints after Activity1 starts
start-equal-finish: Activity2 starts exactly lag timepoints after Activity1 finishes
finish-equal-start: Activity2 finishes exactly lag timepoints after Activity1 starts
finish-equal-finish : Activity2 finishes exactly lag timepoints after Activity1 finishes
The subtypes of Replacement are:
Substitution: This is a one for one replacement. E.g. Activity 1 is no longer valid and has been replaced by Activity 1A
Division: This is a one for many replacement. E.g. Activity 1 is no longer valid and has been replaced by Activities 1A, 1B and 1C
Fusion: This is a many for one replacement. E.g. Activities 1A, 1B and 1C are no longer valid and have been replaced by Activity 1Z</rdf:label>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

